markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Cybersecurity and Global Impacts Unit Overview
 
Teachers can use the Cybersecurity and Global Impacts Unit as part of the AI Foundations course, or as a standalone resource for grades 9-12. It can also be integrated into existing computer science, math, or science curricula, offering scheduling flexibility.

<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-family: Geist, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <p>Students will:</p>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Learn how <strong>computing innovations</strong> have impacted our world in beneficial and harmful ways.</li>
      <li>Learn how <strong>data</strong> can pose a threat to our privacy and security and the ways that encryption and other techniques are used to protect it.</li>
      <li>Participate in a <strong>"school of the future"</strong> conference in which you and a team make a proposal for how best to improve school life with computing innovations.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/c1d4fc3061ce15ad22ce124dd8ebf2e6-Screenshot 2025-04-18 at 10.51.37 AM.png" 
         alt="Computer icon" 
         style="width: 300px; height: auto; border-radius: 10px;margin: 10px">
  </div>
</div>

---

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

## Unit Calendar 

Take a quick look at the lessons included in this unit using the calendar tool.

This version of the calendar shows the pacing for 45 minute class periods and can be customized using the drop-down menu to accommodate your schedule. 

Check out the <a href="https://studio.code.org/s/aif5-2025" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">calendar feature</a> on top of the unit preview. 


<div style="clear:both;"></div>

